   "say": "Reverse a list by flipping every arrow. Start with one, two, three. Keep a pointer called prev, starting at null. Step one, head is one. Save its next, then point one back at prev, which is null. Now prev moves to one, and head moves to two. Step two: point two back at one. Step three: point three back at two. Head runs off the end, so return prev: three, two, one. One pass, O of n time, O of one memory. Save the next pointer first, or you lose the rest."
