   "say": "Cycle detection uses the same trick. If a list loops back on itself, a plain walk never ends. Here five points back to two. Slow takes one step, fast takes two. Round one: slow at two, fast at three. Round two: slow three, fast five. Round three: slow four, fast back at three. Round four: slow five, fast five. They meet. Meeting proves there is a loop, like runners on a circular track. No meeting means fast hit null."
  },
  {
   "type": "code",
   "head": "Both in C plus plus",
   "panels": [
    {
     "file": "sol.cpp",
     "code": "Node* middle(Node* head) {\n    Node *slow = head, *fast = head;\n    while (fast && fast->next) {\n        slow = slow->next;\n        fast = fast->next->next;\n    }\n    return slow;\n}\nbool hasCycle(Node* head) {\n    Node *slow = head, *fast = head;\n    while (fast && fast->next) {\n        slow = slow->next; fast = fast->next->next;\n        if (slow == fast) return true;\n    }\n    return false;\n}"
    }
   ],
